   "he": "נִפְרְצָה בַּלַּיְלָה אוֹ שֶׁפְּרָצוּהָ לִסְטִים כּוּ׳. אָמַר רַבָּה: וְהוּא שֶׁחָתְרָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If the pen «was breached at night, or bandits breached it,» and sheep subsequently went out and caused damage, the owner of the sheep is exempt. «Rabba says: And this» first instance of a pen that was breached is referring specifically to a case «where» the animal «tunneled» under the wall of the pen and by doing so caused the wall to collapse. In that case, the owner is completely blameless and therefore exempt from liability for any damage that ensues."
  }
